      "image": null,
      "weight": 1
     }
    ],
    "attempts": 0,
    "importance": 65,
    "summary": "A study tracking over 3,000 participants revealed that providing direct access to AI-generated answers nearly eliminated their willingness to admit ignorance. Even when the provided AI responses were incorrect, willingness to say 'I don't know' dropped sharply from 44% to 3%.",
